==English==

===Etymology===
From Arabic {{Arab|[[حديث]]}} (''ħadí:θ'', 'Prophetic tradition') < {{Arab|[[حدث]]}} (''ħáddaθa'', 'to tell,' 'to relate,' 'to report').

===Noun===
'''hadith'''  (''plural:'' ''hadith'' or ''hadiths'')

# {{Islam}} the [[collected]] [[saying]]s and [[action]]s of [[Muhammad]] and his companions; used to [[determine]] the [[Sunna]] ([[Muslim]] way of life).

====Translations====
* Arabic: {{Arab|[[حديث]]}} (ħadí:θ) {{m}}
* Kurdish: [[hedîs]] {{f}}

